WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:01.760
Why are my memories...

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:04.060
I really didn't want to die!

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.860
Why is it?
Why am I feeling these things?

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:10.860
What exactly did I do
when I was alive?!

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:14.930
Takuto?

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:18.200
What's the matter, Takuto?

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:19.400
Shut up!

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.300
Please leave me alone!

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.300
Takuto!

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:14.460
Izumi, will you hear me out?

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:17.400
I never thought it
would be so painful

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:20.000
to keep that girl alive for
the duration of her life span.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:28.130
But Takuto doesn't understand
how I feel at all.

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:34.760
Well, it's our job to
adhere to the schedule,

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:38.430
but do you want me to
fix that problem for you?

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:41.760
What do you mean?

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:47.460
I would reap that girl's life
in your place.

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:48.230
What?

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:47.500
You're awake, Mikki?

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:53.860
Long time no see.

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:59.600
What's the matter?
Did you forget my name?

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:08.930
Poor Mikki.
No one can save you now.

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:17.730
I'll take you to the world where
your parents and Eichi are.

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:20.900
Eichi...

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:23.400
That's right.
Don't you want to see him?

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:30.530
Come, follow me.

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:00.560
<i>What has happened to me?</i>

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:04.960
<i>That's my memory from</i>
<i>when I was alive.</i>

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:08.300
<i>Why, all of a sudden?</i>

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:21.030
<i>I just wanted her to sing one more time.</i>
<i>That's all I wanted.</i>

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:25.130
<i>Takuto?</i>

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:28.760
<i>I like your singing, Takuto.</i>

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.760
<i>Hey Takuto,</i>
<i>what kind of songs did you sing?</i>

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:39.400
It's happening again!

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:42.760
Why does this happen
when I think about singing?

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:47.100
Why... Why is this happening?

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:00.500
My...throat?

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:20.500
<i>We'll have to resort to surgery.</i>

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:24.630
<i>No, he won't be able to sing again.</i>

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:44.660
<i>I remember... I used to sing.</i>

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:48.430
<i>But a tumor formed in my lungs.</i>

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:58.330
<i>And I sped off on my motorcycle</i>
<i>out of despair. And I died.</i>

00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:01.230
Damn it!

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:04.030
I can't believe I died.

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:07.200
I... I...

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:17.800
That was great, wasn't it?

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:18.830
Yeah.

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:20.460
They sure know how to perform.

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:21.730
We've gotta work hard to catch up!

00:07:32.530 --> 00:07:34.900
I used to sing.

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:37.030
By myself?

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:39.660
Or in a group?

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:48.830
<i>Takuto!</i>

00:08:01.930 --> 00:08:02.600
<i>Takuto.</i>

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:10.700
Wakaoji...

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:13.830
No way!

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:26.160
<i>The world where Eichi</i>
<i>and my parents are.</i>

00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:29.430
<i>Where is that?</i>

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:37.430
Tonight is the new moon,

00:08:37.460 --> 00:08:39.660
but the moon is there even though
you might not be able to see it.

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:42.500
Didn't Eichi teach you that?

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:46.800
And that Eichi, your mom,
and your dad...

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:50.130
All the people that you want
to see are in the moon.

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:51.700
In the moon?

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:54.360
Not only them.

00:08:55.160 --> 00:08:56.630
There are also animals
in the moon too.

00:08:57.160 --> 00:09:02.060
Like the mochi-making
rabbit and cats too.

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:07.100
There's an African mythology
that goes like this.

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:12.100
Long ago, God tried to bestow
eternal life to humans

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:14.060
and sent a rabbit
as a messenger.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:19.000
But the rabbit opposed the idea, saying,
"Humans are supposed to die."

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:23.700
So God got mad and locked
the rabbit in the moon.

00:09:26.060 --> 00:09:30.700
Rabbits have always been a little dumb.
I guess that's what makes them cute.

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:32.700
Don't you agree?

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:36.360
Now...

00:09:40.060 --> 00:09:41.600
That's a good girl.

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:54.900
<i>I depended on Izumi</i>
<i>without thinking.</i>

00:09:56.200 --> 00:10:00.360
<i>But right now, Izumi might be</i>
<i>doing what he said he'd do.</i>

00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:11.360
<i>Maybe I shouldn't have run away</i>
<i>just because it was so tough.</i>

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:14.900
<i>The one who's suffering</i>
<i>the most is her.</i>

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:20.830
<i>Eichi died two years ago.</i>

00:10:21.130 --> 00:10:21.800
<i>Huh?</i>

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:26.630
<i>My son and daughter-in-law</i>
<i>adopted Eichi,</i>

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:28.960
<i>but all three of them died</i>
<i>in an automobile accident.</i>

00:10:31.260 --> 00:10:33.600
<i>He...died?</i>

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:42.160
<i>But I just couldn't watch her</i>
<i>like that anymore.</i>

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:50.800
<i>But it would be cruel to force her</i>
<i>to continue living in this state.</i>

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:57.530
<i>This is the first time I've had to deal with...</i>
<i>such an exhausting case.</i>

00:10:57.830 --> 00:10:58.900
<i>That's not true!</i>

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:01.700
<i>Even if her life is short,</i>

00:11:01.730 --> 00:11:07.460
<i>making her feel that it was worth living</i>
<i>is part of our job too, right?!</i>

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:11.460
<i>What was I supposed to do?</i>

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:16.730
<i>I'm so lonely without you, Meroko.</i>

00:11:18.830 --> 00:11:23.800
<i>Without you, Meroko, it's like</i>
<i>there's something missing...</i>

00:11:23.830 --> 00:11:25.160
<i>like something's different.</i>

00:11:25.900 --> 00:11:27.230
<i>We have to be together.</i>

00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:30.760
<i>If the three of us aren't together</i>
<i>like we used to be, it'll be sad.</i>

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:33.530
<i>So let's go home together!</i>

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:44.930
<i>Here you go.</i>

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:46.260
<i>It's cute!</i>

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:49.260
<i>You and Takuto are</i>
<i>my precious friends.</i>

00:11:50.300 --> 00:11:51.900
<i>I love you so much, Meroko!</i>

00:11:58.300 --> 00:11:59.300
Mitsuki...

00:12:09.730 --> 00:12:10.730
Mitsuki...

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:17.900
Mitsuki!

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:20.400
Mitsuki!

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:03.330
Maybe I'll tell you another story
about the moon.

00:13:04.900 --> 00:13:08.300
Do you know why the moon
waxes and wanes?

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:14.800
The other gods were jealous
of the moon goddess's beauty.

00:13:15.660 --> 00:13:21.530
Fearing that people's hearts would never
turn to them if the moon were always full,

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:24.030
they made an agreement.

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:31.000
They promised her eternal beauty
if she would go away every so often.

00:13:32.260 --> 00:13:35.330
So the moon also
symbolizes eternity.

00:13:36.430 --> 00:13:39.500
Everybody's existence
is eternal in the moon.

00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:58.530
Welcome to the world
of the eternal moon.

00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:05.860
<i>Takuto.</i>

00:14:08.060 --> 00:14:13.900
<i>Wakaoji... No, Keichi,</i>
<i>I finally remember you.</i>

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:18.230
<i>You, me,</i>
<i>and Mitsuki's father Aoi.</i>

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:20.760
<i>I remember the days when</i>
<i>we used to play together.</i>

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:25.460
<i>Route L... The place</i>
<i>where I started singing...</i>

00:14:26.060 --> 00:14:30.460
<i>And the place that took me in</i>
<i>when I had no relatives.</i>

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:34.600
<i>That feeling that I felt back then...</i>

00:14:35.300 --> 00:14:38.760
<i>It was because I was able to see</i>
<i>what was important to me again.</i>

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:44.030
<i>I'm regretting the fact</i>
<i>that I died!</i>

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:47.860
<i>I should have lived,</i>
<i>more strongly!</i>

00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:50.000
<i>Mitsuki...</i>

00:14:51.060 --> 00:14:52.400
<i>I don't care if I become a ghost!</i>

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:56.730
<i>I won't allow her to have the same</i>
<i>kind of regrets that I have!</i>

00:15:06.560 --> 00:15:07.830
Now, come.

00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:09.300
Mikki!

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:26.400
Look down below.

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:35.360
Eichi?

00:15:36.100 --> 00:15:39.330
And your dad and mom.

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:42.860
My dad and mom...

00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:46.700
I told you, the moon is there
even if you don't see it in the sky.

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:51.000
And that's the entrance
to the world of the moon.

00:15:51.900 --> 00:15:53.930
<i>Mitsuki, I missed you!</i>

00:15:55.400 --> 00:16:00.700
<i>Mitsuki, I have so much to tell you.</i>
<i>Hurry over here.</i>

00:16:02.260 --> 00:16:08.130
<i>Mitsuki, you've grown so much.</i>
<i>Come and show me your face!</i>

00:16:09.030 --> 00:16:14.700
Dad, mom, Eichi...
I missed you.

00:16:16.030 --> 00:16:18.160
I wanted to see you so badly.

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:25.900
Dad?

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:27.330
Mom?

00:16:28.060 --> 00:16:30.030
<i>Mitsuki, goodbye.</i>

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:31.400
No.

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:34.630
No, Eichi.

00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:36.460
Don't leave.

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:49.860
Now, Mikki, let's go together to
the world of the eternal moon.

00:16:55.500 --> 00:16:56.500
Mitsuki!

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:02.160
Who?

00:17:03.100 --> 00:17:04.100
Getting in the way...

00:17:04.360 --> 00:17:08.430
Get off of there now!
It's dangerous! Now!

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:11.100
Don't think of killing yourself!

00:17:11.860 --> 00:17:12.530
<i>Kill myself?</i>

00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:19.300
<i>But I'm just going to go see</i>
<i>Eichi and my dad and mom.</i>

00:17:24.460 --> 00:17:25.460
<i>Where?</i>

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:31.030
Please, Mitsuki!

00:17:33.500 --> 00:17:36.030
Please just come over here!

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:41.400
If I let you die, Hazuki and your father
will never forgive me!

00:17:42.300 --> 00:17:47.100
No!
I-I don't want you to die!

00:17:48.030 --> 00:17:50.400
I don't want anybody
to die anymore.

00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:56.730
Please, just come back!

00:17:57.900 --> 00:17:58.900
Mitsuki!

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:04.260
Grandma?

00:18:04.730 --> 00:18:07.900
In that case,
I guess I'll have to be a little rough.

00:18:10.700 --> 00:18:14.160
That's right. It's Grandma.
So please get over here right away.

00:18:17.800 --> 00:18:18.800
Grandma?

00:18:35.330 --> 00:18:36.330
Grandma...

00:18:36.500 --> 00:18:38.700
Mitsuki, come on!

00:19:11.200 --> 00:19:12.330
Grandma!

00:19:14.360 --> 00:19:15.030
No!

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:17.330
It's useless. It's too late.

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:19.800
Grandma! Grandma!

00:19:19.860 --> 00:19:21.260
Grandma!

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:23.060
What's too late?

00:19:32.060 --> 00:19:33.060
Takuto!

00:19:35.530 --> 00:19:36.530
Grandma!

00:19:36.930 --> 00:19:39.230
Don't worry.
She just fainted.

00:19:41.600 --> 00:19:45.030
Izumi, you little...
I'm not going to forgive you this time!

00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:46.900
Don't get so mad.

00:19:47.860 --> 00:19:50.360
It's not entirely my fault this time.

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:51.660
What?!

00:19:52.160 --> 00:19:54.000
He's right. It's my fault.

00:19:55.600 --> 00:20:00.000
This all started because
I depended on Izumi.

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:01.630
I told you.

00:20:02.060 --> 00:20:02.730
But...

00:20:03.400 --> 00:20:09.600
I was wrong! Even if we are Death Spirits,
we can't do things like this!

00:20:14.200 --> 00:20:20.160
Mitsuki, you had to go through such
a scary experience because of me.

00:20:23.800 --> 00:20:24.460
I'm sorry!

00:20:31.930 --> 00:20:33.100
Mitsuki...

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:39.630
Oh boy, now I'm the bad guy.

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:46.160
I was just trying to take
her soul for you Meroko.

00:20:48.230 --> 00:20:51.230
This is why I shouldn't butt
into people's business.

00:20:51.630 --> 00:20:53.160
Izumi...

00:20:53.200 --> 00:20:56.930
More importantly, you remember
all of it now, right, Takuto?

00:20:58.760 --> 00:21:03.660
Or should I call you
Takuto Kira of Route L?

00:21:07.100 --> 00:21:09.060
Y-You! How did you know that?!

00:21:10.360 --> 00:21:14.560
I'd love to hear you sing
one of these days

00:21:15.760 --> 00:21:17.460
before you become a ghost.

00:21:21.630 --> 00:21:24.530
<i>Takuto, do you remember</i>
<i>your past now?</i>

00:21:25.500 --> 00:21:29.960
<i>Route L?</i>
<i>Dad and Dr. Wakaoji's band?</i>

00:23:06.600 --> 00:23:10.930
I remember. When I was a human,
I was in Route L.

00:23:10.960 --> 00:23:13.500
Takuto, your memories
have returned?

00:23:13.860 --> 00:23:16.700
No! You have to forget them right away!
Or else something bad will happen!

00:23:16.730 --> 00:23:17.400
It's fine.

00:23:18.160 --> 00:23:22.200
If the return of my memories
causes her to want sing again,

00:23:22.660 --> 00:23:24.130
I want to remember everything.

00:23:24.460 --> 00:23:27.060
Takuto, no! Takuto!

00:23:28.060 --> 00:23:31.560
Next time on Full Moon:
"New Moon Night."

00:23:32.100 --> 00:23:33.100
- Look forward to it!
- Look forward to it!
